===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# At an earlier time.
#: {{syn|en|previously}}
#: {{ant|en|after}}
#: {{ux|en|I've never done this '''before'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|This achievement far exceeded anything that had come '''before'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Maxwell Mirror and the Lamp|chapter=12|passage=All this was extraordinarily distasteful to Churchill. It was ugly, gross. Never '''before''' had he felt such repulsion when the vicar displayed his characteristic bluntness or coarseness of speech. In the present connexion—or rather as a transition from the subject that started their conversation—such talk had been distressingly out of place.}}
# {{lb|en|chiefly literary or poetic}} In advance in position or sequence; ahead.
#: {{syn|en|ahead}}
#: {{ux|en|We walked behind while they went '''before'''.}}
# {{lb|en|uncommon}} At the front end.
#: {{syn|en|in front}}
#: {{ant|en|behind}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1896|author=w:Hilaire Belloc|title=The Bad Child’s Book of Beasts|chapter=[[s:The Bad Child's Book Of Beasts/The Elephant|The Elephant]]
|passage=When people call this beast to mind,<br/>They marvel more and more<br/>At such a {{smallcaps|little}} tail behind,<br/>So <big>LARGE</big> a trunk '''before'''.}}

